{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Do not entreat me</b> [אל תפגעי בי]. The meaning is appeasement, and it is always joined with a bet, like <b>and entreat for me with Ephron</b> [ופגעו לי בעפרון]. And there is no foreign word; only <b>I will not entreat a person</b> [לא אפגע אדם] — in its place I will explain it." "<b>Your people is my people</b> [עמך עמי]. I will never abandon the Torah of Israel and the unity of the Name."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Genesis 50:4, where the phrase is ופגעו לי בעפרון; he cites it to show פגע joined with ב."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:22.126549926Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}